    "title": "Local man accused of dumping 3 tons of trash - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n5 hours ago\nKEY LARGO — A 53-year-old local man was arrested on Wednesday, Nov. 26, for allegedly illegally dumping more than 6,000 pounds of trash, furniture and household items on a Monroe County-owned property in Key Largo.\nThe Monroe County Sheriff’s Office said William Montano Balmaceda is charged with illegally dumping the debris at the Monroe County Housing Authority property at Harry Davis Circle in Key Largo.\n“Montano Balmaceda dumped 6,640 pounds of debris/trash that included, but not limited to, household garbage, couches, plywood, chairs, metal, glass, appliances, lawn equipment, bicycles and vehicle parts,” MCSO said in a statement.\nMontano Balmaceda allegedly told deputies he removed the trash after being warned several times, but never did.\nSheriff's office personnel and county workers removed the trash during a community clean up effort on Nov. 18.\nA warrant was obtained for Montano Balmaceda’s arrest and he was booked into jail.",
